# Lessons

## User Specified Lessons
- You have a python venv in ./venv. Use it.
- Include info useful for debugging in the program output.
- Read the file before you try to edit it.
- Due to Cursor's limit, when you use `git` and `gh` and need to submit a multiline commit message, first write the message in a file, and then use `git commit -F <filename>` or similar command to commit. And then remove the file. Include "[Cursor] " in the commit message and PR title.

## Cursor learned
- For search results, ensure proper handling of different character encodings (UTF-8) for international queries
- Add debug information to stderr while keeping the main output clean in stdout for better pipeline integration
- When using seaborn styles in matplotlib, use 'seaborn-v0_8' instead of 'seaborn' as the style name due to recent seaborn version changes
- Use 'gpt-4o' as the model name for OpenAI's GPT-4 with vision capabilities
- Dora (legacy, `Dora/`) is the old SwiftUI prototype; Fenestra (`Fenestra/` + `Packages/`) is the real app. Build Fenestra with `make build` / `xcodegen generate`.
- File explorer apps keep App Sandbox off for free filesystem browse.
- KeyCatcherView/NSView must not steal firstResponder from NSTextField/NSTextView.
- **Package.swift platform**: `.macOS(.v26)` does not exist in PackageDescription here; use `.macOS("26.0")`.
- **Drop `InternalImportsByDefault`** for now: it forces `public import` on every type that leaks. Add back per-package once APIs are stable.
- **C macros import as `UInt32`** (`ATTR_CMN_*`, `VDIR`, …) while `obj_type_t` is `UInt32`. Never compare a macro straight to `UInt32(VDIR.rawValue)` without a cast; that bit us.
- **`getattrlistbulk` in-process is unreliable here**: first call returns a partial batch with a 4-byte `f_getattrlist` prefix; later calls on the same fd return a malformed stale buffer that loops forever. Design: one bulk call, then `readdir`+`lstat` for the remainder. Standalone binaries on the same machine behaved differently — do not assume.
- **`Darwin.statfs`** name collides with the `statfs` struct inside a type; use `getmntinfo(3)` for mount info instead.
- **No `NSGlassEffectView`** exists. Use `NSVisualEffectView` (titlebar/sidebar/hudWindow) + SwiftUI `.glassEffect` and fall back to opaque under Reduce Transparency.
- `URLResourceKey` has no `volumeIsNetworkKey`/`volumeFileSystemTypeKey`; use `volumeIsLocalKey` + `getmntinfo`.
- `OSSignpostIntervalState` has no public `.id`; create `OSSignpostID(log:)` yourself and pass it to `beginInterval(_:id:)`.
- `.localizedStandardCompare` is **not** natural-numeric in this SDK ("file 10" < "file 2"); implement digit-run comparison manually.
- XcodeGen: `mkdir -p a/{b,c}` does not brace-expand in zsh; create dirs explicitly (`perl -e 'File::Path::make_path'` or one path per command).

# Scratchpad

## Current task
Fenestra — native macOS 26 file explorer (Windows 11 Explorer parity). Prompt-by-prompt.

## Plan (prompts 0–19)
[X] P0 scaffold — 8 SPM packages, AppKit app, tests, CI, Makefile
[X] P1 FSCore — FileItem, bulk enumerator (+readdir fallback), FSEvents watcher, DirectoryModel, VolumeService, sort/group + tests; 100k first batch 19.8 ms
[ ] P2 window shell — tab strip in title bar, nav bar, command bar, split view, status bar, glass, per-tab state, restore
[ ] P3 Details view — NSTableView, columns/sort/groups/selection/rename/context menu, per-folder view memory
[ ] Review pass 0–3

## Decisions
- Bundle ID `com.dorasoft.fenestra`, ad-hoc signing until a team ID is supplied.
- Keep `Dora/` as reference; do not delete.
- macOS 26 + arm64 only. Timing-sensitive perf tests are local-only.
- F2 on 1 item = inline rename; F2 on 2+ = PowerRename sheet (resolves prompt 3 vs 16 conflict).
